==Strategy==
Because the Celeboodles don't have too much health yet come with a relatively high money drop, money is not going to be a factor, so feel free to use expensive, spammable [[:Category:Area Attack Cats|Area Attackers]] such as [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Paris Cat]], [[Bird Cat (Normal Cat)|The Flying Cat]], [[Crazed Bird Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed UFO Cat]] or [[Wheel Cat (Rare Cat)|Solar Cat]]. [[Pogo Cat (Rare Cat)|Jiangshi Cat]] is a great meatshield here to use since it is essentially two meatshields in one and its price can be overlooked here. It helps to bring in a Cat CPU. Spamming your attackers can overwhelm them quickly due to their low health, preventing them from causing too much damage, and defeating them quickly restocks your funds, allowing even more attackers if the enemies managed to demolish some of yours.

Stall the first Shibaliens until your wallet is completely maxed, then start spamming all your Area Attackers. You need to make sure to summon enough meatshields to keep the Celeboodles from attacking your attackers while getting enough attackers to kill them. Eventually, the finite Celeboodles will be exhausted to sparse spawns, allowing you to easily finish the stage.

